<article class="env-lemma" id="01N2">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01N2">Lemma <span data-tag="01N2">27.11.6</span>.</a> With hypotheses and notation as in Lemma <a href="/tag/01MY" data-tag="01MY">27.11.1</a> above. Assume there exists a ring map $R \to A_0$ and a ring map $R \to R'$ such that $B = R' \otimes _ R A$. Then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$U(\psi ) = Y$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ Y = \text{Proj}(B) \ar[r]_{r_\psi } \ar[d] &  \text{Proj}(A) = X \ar[d] \\  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R') \ar[r] &  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R) }  \]
</div>
<p>
 is a fibre product square, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the maps $\theta : r_\psi ^*\mathcal{O}_ X(n) \to \mathcal{O}_ Y(n)$ are isomorphisms. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately by looking at what happens over the standard opens $D_{+}(f)$ for $f \in A_{+}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>